@startuml
title 2B - GitHub: the agent is tagged on a foreign PR\nThe tag is the mandate, and it is what the machine sees

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Human
participant GitHub
participant "GitHubAdapter" as GA
participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "Store" as S
participant "SandboxPool" as P
participant "WorkerRunner\n(sandbox)" as R

Human -> GitHub: comment "@<agent_login> ..." on a PR we did not open
GitHub -> GA: webhook issue_comment/created
GA -> O: OnPrComment{pr:repo#n, mentionsUs, isDraft, isMerged}
note right of O
  The adapter reports the comment and its facts.
  Whether a tag is a mandate is decided in the machine:
  it opens an instance when the comment tags us and the
  PR is not merged.
end note
O -> S: create PrMaintainer instance
return prm_pending

loop while the PR is open
  O -> P: enqueue SandboxRun(PrMaintainer)
  O -> S: state
  return prm_working
  P -> R: execute
  R -> GitHub: reply threads / fix CI / push
  return replies, head_sha
  R -> P: result
  P -> O: run finished
  alt attempts left and work remains
    O -> S: state
    return prm_waiting
  else attempts exhausted
    O -> S: state
    return prm_attempts_exhausted
  end
  GitHub -> GA: next event (checks, review, push)
  GA -> O: GitHubRequest
  note right of O
    Admitted because the INSTANCE exists, not because
    each event re-passes the tag test.
  end note
end
GitHub -> GA: pull_request/closed (merged)
GA -> O: GitHubRequest
O -> S: state
return prm_merged

note right of O
  On OUR PRs none of this needs asking: the sweep already
  announces them, so following them is the default.
end note
@enduml
